# Copy to /etc/heresay/notify.env, fill in real values, then: chmod 600 it.
#
# ⛔ NEVER COMMIT THE REAL FILE. Both values are secrets in the only sense that
# matters — knowing one IS the permission:
#
#   - the ntfy topic is the ONLY auth on public ntfy.sh, so anyone who learns it
#     can read every alert you send and post alerts that look like yours;
#   - the Healthchecks URL lets anyone ping (or forge) your dead-man's-switch,
#     which means silencing the alarm that says your backups stopped.
#
# This .example ships placeholders only, and the install step will NOT overwrite
# an existing notify.env. Same discipline as the fail2ban jail, which ships
# loopback-only and never an operator's real address.

# ntfy push target. Use a long, UNGUESSABLE topic — it is the only auth on
# public ntfy.sh. Generate one with:
#   echo "heresay-$(head -c 9 /dev/urandom | base32 | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]' | tr -d '=')"
NTFY_URL=https://ntfy.sh/CHANGE-ME-to-an-unguessable-topic

# Healthchecks.io ping URL for the backup dead-man's-switch (the check's ping URL).
# Leave blank to disable the backup ping.
HC_BACKUP_URL=https://hc-ping.com/CHANGE-ME-your-check-uuid
